===== VERDICT: PHASE 4 FAIL =====

TOTAL_HITS = 0, BANK_STATUS did not toggle, PORT_STATUS = 0xFF throughout.
Same symptom as prior Phase 4 test with fix-runctl-reset-260511 SOF.

Root cause analysis:
  - hist-debug-disconnect (removing 6 AVST taps) did NOT fix PORT_STATUS=0xFF.
  - Both runctl_mgmt_host_0 LOCAL_CMD and dbg_mm2runctrl HOST_CMD injections
    confirmed the RUNNING state reached the run_control_splitter AVST input.
  - Yet PORT_STATUS stayed 0xFF (all 8 ingress FIFOs empty on histogram).
  - This confirms the rc-readyless rollout (commit 17e0cec8) is needed:
    the auto-inserted timing_adapters on run_control_splitter outputs are
    blocking the RC_RUNNING broadcast to the emulators.
  - rc-readyless fix: sink USE_READY=0 eliminates auto-inserted adapters,
    allows the splitter broadcast to reach emulator asi_ctrl unconditionally.

Next action: rc-readyless bundled recompile (pending mutrig_frame_deassembly
IP fix by parallel Sonnet subagent) -> Phase 4 retest as phase4_postfix2.

Note on LVDS link: LINK_LOCKED_LOW bit 2 = 0 (FEB LVDS link not locked on SWB).
This is a separate issue from the PORT_STATUS=0xFF symptom. The rc_tool reset-link
path did not work in this session. LOCAL_CMD SC write was used as the fallback
run-control injection path. The LVDS lock issue may resolve after the rc-readyless
compile (different timing on xcvr signals) or may require separate investigation.
